          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "testāmentum, testāmentī — \"a will, a testament\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Senex testāmentum cōram testibus scrīpsit. The old man wrote his will in front of witnesses."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter, from a verb meaning 'to call to witness', and so from testis (taught). Seven witnesses sealed a Roman will."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "testāmentum is built on testor, \"to call to witness\", from testis, \"witness\" (EtymDB): a declaration made before witnesses. English testament comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
