              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "relinquō, relinquere — \"to leave behind; to leave (in a will)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pater fīliīs domum et agrōs relīquit. The father left the house and the fields to his sons."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "relinquō, relinquere, relīquī, relictum. English relinquish and relic belong to its family."
            }
          ]
        },
