          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "relinquō is built on linquō, \"to leave\", with re-, \"back, behind\" (EtymDB). English relinquish comes from it through French, and relic from reliquiae, \"remains\", of the same family."
            }
          ]
        },
